     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Tahoma,Tahoma;font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span><br>Hi Perry :<br> </span>I was a bit surprised when trying to run a code in nimble: The data is a</div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Tahoma,Tahoma;font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">1176*35 RH matrix. I get the message: error:impossible to allocate a vector</div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Tahoma,Tahoma;font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"> of 12.3 Go.Warning messages:</div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Tahoma,Tahoma;font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"> 1: In integer(maxNewEdges) : Reached total allocation of 12287Mb: see</div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Tahoma,Tahoma;font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"> help(memory.size).</div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Tahoma,Tahoma;font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"> This code runs fine under Win7 64 bits and R64 with jags ; also</div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Tahoma,Tahoma;font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"> in nimble when data is a 587*12 matrix with only a warning related to memory. I&#39;ve tried to increase memory</div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Tahoma,Tahoma;font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"> through memory.limit(size=50000) but with no success.</div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Tahoma,Tahoma;font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"> In R help I&#39;ve seen: It is not normally possible to allocate as much as</div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Tahoma,Tahoma;font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"> 2Gb to a single vector in a 32-bit build of R even on 64-bit Windows because</div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Tahoma,Tahoma;font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"> of preallocations by  Windows in the middle of the address space. But is</div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Tahoma,Tahoma;font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"> this relevant? <br>I have attached  the code in question, but not the data file itself.<br></div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Tahoma,Tahoma;font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"> I would be very pleased if you could help, many thanks,<br>Gilbert.<br></div></div>"
