     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\">Hi Gilbert,<div><br></div><div>Thanks for this reproducible example.  The problem has to do with a step of internal processing where the case of very high numbers of edges (relationships between nodes) explodes the size of an R object used in the processing.  I believe I have it fixed, but I’ll have to ask you to install from a github branch to try it.  There is a subsequent processing issue raised by your example that I’m also fixing.  I’ll let you know when I have something ready for you to try.  In addition there are ways your model can be written more compactly in nimble that I will send along.  I just wanted to give you an update for the moment.</div><div><br></div><div>Perry</div><div><br><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div>On Jan 28, 2016, at 2:59 AM, GMarzolin &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">gmar...@numericable.fr</a>&gt; wrote:</div><br><div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:18px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"></div></div></blockquote></div></div></div>"
